  "_notes": {
    "Sw_override": "Plasma-facing surface area [m^2] for real machines (APPROX, confirm vs published). W7-X ~128 and LHD ~120 from published plasma-surface estimates; HSX 9.1 and CFQS 12.6 estimated from 2*pi*R0 * 2*pi*a * sqrt((1+kappa^2)/2) with kappa~1.5. Anchors Pwall=(Pfus+Pheat)/Sw instead of the extreme near-axis elongation profile (e.g. HSX elongation ~384). Concept reactors (HELIAS, NAE-QA) keep Sw_override=0 (pure near-axis). See docs/39.",
    "etabar": "For measured machines (W7-X/LHD/HSX/CFQS) etabar is chosen for a REPRESENTATIVE near-axis cross-section only (modest elongation); the transform/volume/wall come from measured iota/Vp_override/Sw_override, so etabar does not affect their power account. Single-harmonic near-axis cannot truly represent these devices.",
    "shape": "Real machines carry an explicit 'shape' = truncated (|m|,|n|<=2), normalized boundary Fourier harmonics from a PUBLIC equilibrium (DESC desc/examples: W7-X, HSX, ESTELL; canonical l=2 heliotron for LHD), evaluated in DESC double-Fourier product basis and rescaled to preset R0 and a=R0/A. Cross-section VIEW only; near-axis cannot represent bean/heliotron/QA. Does NOT affect power account (iota/Vp/Sw measured). Truncated cartoon, not a full equilibrium."
  },
